# =============================================================================
# Trivy ignore list — accepted base-image vulnerabilities
# =============================================================================
# The relay and ui images share the python:3.12-slim-bookworm (Debian 12) base.
# The CRITICAL CVEs below have NO fixed Debian version available, so they cannot
# be resolved by patching, `apt-get upgrade`, or rebasing onto a newer base-image
# digest. They are accepted as documented risk — see the "Known Accepted Risks"
# section in SECURITY.md for the full rationale.
#
# This file is auto-loaded by Trivy from the repository root, so a scan
# configured to fail on CRITICAL findings passes with the acceptance recorded
# in version control. Re-review when Debian ships fixes and drop resolved entries.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-07-02
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# zlib1g — integer overflow in minizip's zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6.
# Debian: will_not_fix. The vulnerable minizip code is not compiled into Debian's
# zlib1g, so the library as shipped is not affected. Never fixed upstream.
CVE-2023-45853

# perl-base — heap buffer overflow compiling regexes on 32-bit builds only.
# Not applicable: images are built for 64-bit platforms. No fix available.
CVE-2026-8376

# perl-base — path traversal in Archive::Tar via crafted symlinks.
# Debian: fix_deferred (no fix yet). Archive::Tar is not used at runtime.
CVE-2026-42496

# libsqlite3-0 — SQLite integer overflow. Status: affected, no fixed Debian
# version available. Re-evaluate once Debian ships a patch.
CVE-2025-7458
